  "summary": "A 12-week, 3-day beginner program that rotates four different full-body workouts, each with three main lifts and two accessories done as a descending-rep pyramid of three sets. This is the hypertrophy variation; the strength variation uses 3-5 / 5-8 / 8-10 on the main lifts, accessories are the same.",
  "evidenceNote": "Stopping 1-2 reps short of failure on every set fits current evidence for beginners, and the pyramid gives both heavy and moderate-rep exposure. Because four workouts rotate over three days, each main lift is trained less than once a week and most muscles get roughly 4-9 hard sets weekly, which is on the low side for hypertrophy but fine for new lifters. No deload or stall rule is given.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Greg Nuckols Beginner Program (Boostcamp, free program page, updated Oct 2026)",
      "url": "https://www.boostcamp.app/greg-nuckols/greg-nuckols-beginner-program",
